{"name":"Denim Tradition","hex":"#7f97b5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"denim","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A textile often made of cotton with a distinct diagonal pattern."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/denim"},{"term":"tradition","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A part of culture that is passed from person to person or generation to generation, possibly differing in detail from family to family, such as the way to celebrate holidays.","A commonly held system. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To transmit by way of tradition; to hand down."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tradition"}],"entries":[{"title":"Denim","blocks":[{"text":"Denim is a sturdy, cotton, warp-faced textile in which the weft passes under two or more warp threads. This twill weave produces a diagonal ribbing that distinguishes it from cotton duck. Denim, as it is recognised today, was first produced in Nîmes, France."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Denim_texture_03.jpg/330px-Denim_texture_03.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Denim","wikidata":"Q652698"},{"title":"Tradition","blocks":[{"text":"A tradition is a system of beliefs or behaviors passed down within a group of people or society with symbolic meaning or special significance with origins in the past. A component of cultural expressions and folklore, common examples include holidays or impractical but socially meaningful clothes, but the idea has also been applied to social norms and behaviors such as greetings. Traditions can persist and evolve for thousands of years. The word tradition itself derives from the Latin word tradere literally meaning to transmit, to hand over, to give for safekeeping. While it is reportedly assumed that traditions have an ancient history, many traditions have been invented on purpose, whether it be political or cultural, over short periods of time. Various academic disciplines also use the word in a variety of ways."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/26/Tradition-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg/330px-Tradition-Warner-Highsmith.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tradition","wikidata":"Q82821"},{"title":"List of colors: A–F","blocks":[{"text":"The following is a list of colors. A number of the color swatches below are taken from domain-specific naming schemes such as X11 or HTML4. RGB values are given for each swatch because such standards are defined in terms of the sRGB color space. It is not possible to accurately convert many of these swatches to CMYK values because of the differing gamuts of the two spaces, but the color management systems built into operating systems and image editing software attempt such conversions as accurately as possible."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Colouring_pencils.jpg/330px-Colouring_pencils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_colors%3A_A%E2%80%93F","wikidata":"Q16912543"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Denim_jacket_cuff_closeup.jpg/500px-Denim_jacket_cuff_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Denim_jacket_cuff_closeup.jpg/1280px-Denim_jacket_cuff_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Denim_jacket_cuff_closeup.jpg/500px-Denim_jacket_cuff_closeup.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Denim fabric dyed with indigo and black dyes and made into a shirt","link":"https://en.wikipedia.or